# Hexplace project

Prefer [`.agents/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`](../docs/ARCHITECTURE.md) and
[README.md](../../README.md) (setup/ops) for domain detail. Use
[AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) only as an index of rules, skills, commands, and
hooks.

## Out of scope (do not invent)

- Planet-scale import, sharding, or multi-shard query routing
- Live minutely / diff replication
- OSM relation import, admin boundaries, or polygon point-in-polygon hierarchy
- House-number interpolation along ways
- Nominatim-style or locale-aware display names
- Learned / population-based / multilingual importance models

## When unsure

- Architecture / “where does X live” → skill `hexplace-architecture`
- Import, PBF, indexes, schema bumps → skill `hexplace-import`
- Before claiming done on Rust work → skill `hexplace-verify` or command `/verify`
